    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "These four documents show how planners first described the Asian audience as a revolution to be won, a public inclined to follow the winner, and a Japanese press to be countered. They follow the thread from the 1949 call for an expanded information program to the 1954 admission that the Tokyo committee was not working."
