      "volumeId": "frus1950v06",
      "documentId": "d32",
      "text": "Both Pignon, the French High Commissioner for Indochina, and MacDonald, Commissioner for the United Kingdom in Southeast Asia, believe that the Asians are inclined by their psychology to wait and see who is winning. The bandwagon attitude will be more important than questions of ideology in determining their decisions."
